VarCon is part of Kevin Atkinson's SCOWL project. It encodes the preferred
American, British ("ise"), British ("ize" / Oxford), Canadian and Australian
spellings of a word, together with variant-status and part-of-speech tags. The
A/B/Z split is what makes a first-class `--oxford` mode possible without a
second hand-maintained word list.

The file is vendored verbatim, byte for byte, so the checksum above can be
verified against upstream. `build.rs` derives a compact lookup table from it at
build time; the file itself is never read at run time.


